Title: Hail, Ergamenes
Order: 15
Production Code: 1x15

INT. TELASSAR - TERRACE - DAY

AMB: fountains, birdsong, a city stirring below

Ai shows Reuel Briggs the hidden city from its highest terrace — an outer and inner city built into a horseshoe curve of mountain, fields and vineyards stretching beyond.

AI
Six thousand years before Christ's birth, this city had already reached its height. Your modern world, I'm told, is still catching up to it in most things that matter.

They descend by palanquin into the city itself, drawn toward a great temple by the sound of a deep bell and a gathering crowd.

INT. TELASSAR - TEMPLE - CONTINUOUS

AMB: stringed instruments, a hush of anticipation

Inside, Council members prostrate themselves before Reuel one by one — among them Ababdis, so transformed by his robes of office as to be almost unrecognizable. Ai, now robed in ceremonial azure, lifts a jeweled crown — its center stone the black diamond of Senechus — and sets it on Reuel's head.

A curtain parts. Reuel finds himself alone on a platform above a vast, packed auditorium, an arch of fire overhead spelling out a single word.

CROWD (V.O.)
(as one, thunderous)
HAIL, ERGAMENES!

REUEL BRIGGS
(stunned, to Ai afterward)
Who is Ergamenes?

AI
Thou art Ergamenes — the long-looked-for king of Ethiopia, for whose reception this city was built.

At the feast that follows, musicians kneel and sing the history of Ergamenes and his kingdom, and Ai names the mark.

AI
Son of a fallen dynasty, outcast of a sunken people, upon your breast is a lotus lily, God's mark to prove your race and descent. You, Ergamenes, shall begin the restoration of Ethiopia.

Reuel listens, and finally understands the birthmark he has carried, unexplained, his entire life.

REUEL BRIGGS (V.O.)
I have carefully hidden my Ethiopian extraction from the world. It was a tradition among those who knew me in childhood that I was descended from a race of African kings. I remember my mother well — her candle at my bedside, the broken prayers as she examined my breast.
